# Line endings. Git on this machine converts LF to CRLF in the working copy,
# which is harmless for Python but fatal for the adapter scripts: a CRLF after
# the shebang makes Linux report "bad interpreter: no such file or directory",
# and the user has no way to guess why. Pin the ones that must stay LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Keep dev-only files out of the tarball the app store downloads onto badges.
# export-ignore only applies to `git archive`, which is how GitHub builds the
# release tarball -- which is exactly what the store fetches.
#
# Never add `boards/` or `LICENSE` here: the first is shipped code, the second
# has to travel with it.
tests/ export-ignore
tools/ export-ignore
docs/ export-ignore
adapters/ export-ignore
Makefile export-ignore
metadata.json export-ignore
.gitignore export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
README.md export-ignore
controls.md export-ignore
CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
SECURITY.md export-ignore
EDGEWISE_SPEC.md export-ignore
